---
import DarkLayout from "../layouts/DarkLayout.astro";
---

<DarkLayout title="Resonara — Our Story" description="Born in Loss. Built with Love. The story of Resonara.">
  <!-- ═══════════ HERO ═══════════ -->
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="bowl-pulse">
      <div class="bp-ring"></div>
      <div class="bp-ring"></div>
      <div class="bp-ring"></div>
      <div class="bp-ring"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="hero-content fade-up">
      <div class="hero-eyebrow">The Origin</div>
      <h1 class="hero-title">Born in <span>Loss</span>.<br />Built with <span>Love</span>.</h1>
      <p class="hero-sub">Resonara did not begin in a lab, or a boardroom, or a pitch deck.<br />It began on the day a family chose to answer a question that grief had asked.</p>
      <div class="hero-date">October 2024 &nbsp;·&nbsp; Singapore</div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══════════ ACT I ═══════════ -->
  <div class="ornament"><span>✦</span></div>

  <section class="prose-section">
    <div class="prose-inner">
      <div class="fade-up">
        <span class="chapter-num">I</span>
        <span class="chapter-label">The Loss</span>
        <h2 class="chapter-title">The mind that could take any market loss<br />could not handle <span>a personal one</span></h2>
      </div>
      <div class="fade-up">
        <p class="body-p">In October 2024, Ajay Sharma lost his father.</p>
        <p class="body-p">
          He had spent twenty-five years in Asian capital markets — reading signals in noise, building frameworks for complexity, staying calm when others could not. The tools were sophisticated. The
          mind was trained. But grief does not respond to analysis. It does not care for frameworks.
        </p>
        <p class="body-p">For the first time in a long time, he did not know what to do with stillness.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="pull-quote fade-up">
        <p>The market can be read. Loss cannot. It must simply be entered — and, somehow, passed through.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="fade-up">
        <p class="body-p">
          His wife Shalini — a PhD in Pharmaceutics, a certified Yoga Therapist, a healer in the truest sense — did not offer a solution. She offered a direction. <em>Go to a sound bath session,</em> she
          said. <em>Just go.</em>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══════════ DATE MARKER ═══════════ -->
  <div class="date-marker fade-up">
    <div class="timeline-spine"></div>
    <div class="date-big">10 November 2024</div>
    <div class="date-sub">Singapore. A single session. Surrounded by many bowls.</div>
  </div>

  <!-- ═══════════ ACT II ═══════════ -->
  <section class="prose-section dark-band">
    <div class="prose-inner">
      <div class="fade-up">
        <span class="chapter-num">II</span>
        <span class="chapter-label">The Frequency</span>
        <h2 class="chapter-title">Something the body already <span>knew</span></h2>
      </div>
      <div class="fade-up">
        <p class="body-p">The session lasted less than an hour. What it produced lingered for days.</p>
        <p class="body-p">
          Not comfort, exactly. Not closure. Something older and quieter than either — a state the mind recognises before it can name it. <em
            >The ancient texts call it Samadhi. The neuroscientists call it deep parasympathetic activation.</em
          > Ajay simply knew he had not felt it before, and needed to feel it again.
        </p>
        <p class="body-p">
          The entrepreneur's question arrived before the session had even ended: <em
            >A gifted practitioner created this. But what about the days between sessions? What about the millions who will never find their way to a room like this?</em
          > Could this frequency also be available every morning, reliably, repeatably — not to replace the human touch, but to extend its reach into the hours and homes where no practitioner can be present?
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="pull-quote fade-up">
        <p>
          The practitioner who led that session gave something irreplaceable. What we wanted was for that gift — that exact quality of resonance — to reach beyond the one room, the one hour, the one
          appointment.
        </p>
        <cite>— Ajay Sharma, Co-Founder</cite>
      </div>
      <div class="fade-up">
        <p class="body-p">
          He wanted to extend the reach of what skilled practitioners had always known. Not to replace them — a gifted sound healer brings intuition, presence, and attunement that no device can
          replicate — but to build something that could carry the practice into the daily life of people who need it most. To make consistent, calibrated resonance available at home, every day,
          between sessions.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══════════ ACT III ═══════════ -->
  <div class="ornament"><span>✦</span></div>

  <section class="prose-section">
    <div class="prose-inner">
      <div class="fade-up">
        <span class="chapter-num">III</span>
        <span class="chapter-label">The Huddle</span>
        <h2 class="chapter-title">A family that <span>already had</span><br />every piece of the answer</h2>
      </div>
      <div class="fade-up">
        <p class="body-p">
          Jayesha was there. Not on a phone call — in Singapore, present in the room that day when her father returned from the session. She had witnessed the shift in him firsthand. A Yoga
          practitioner who had long lived at the intersection of ancient practice and modern science, she did not need to be convinced. She simply said: <em>"Let's build it."</em>
        </p>
        <p class="body-p">
          On November 10th, 2024, the three of them — Ajay, Shalini, Jayesha — sat together and made a commitment. Over the next few months, they took a deep dive into the science: acoustic physics,
          EEG brainwave entrainment, HRV biometric studies, the metallurgy of Himalayan bowls, the centuries of Vedic documentation on nāda yoga. The more they read, the more certain they became. The
          mechanism was real. The tradition was real. What was missing was precision engineering.
        </p>
        <p class="body-p">They found two more people who could build what they could see.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══════════ STAT BAR ═══════════ -->
  <div class="prose-section" style="padding-top:0; padding-bottom: clamp(3rem,6vw,5rem);">
    <div class="stat-bar fade-up">
      <div class="stat-item">
        <span class="stat-val">1</span>
        <span class="stat-label">Session that changed everything</span>
      </div>
      <div class="stat-item">
        <span class="stat-val">3</span>
        <span class="stat-label">Founders. One family's vision.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="stat-item">
        <span class="stat-val">3,000+</span>
        <span class="stat-label">Years of Vedic sound tradition</span>
      </div>
      <div class="stat-item">
        <span class="stat-val">3</span>
        <span class="stat-label">Patents filed &amp; pending</span>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- ═══════════ FOUNDERS ═══════════ -->
  <section class="team-section">
    <div class="team-header fade-up">
      <div class="section-label">The Founders and the Craftsmen</div>
      <h2 class="section-heading">Five people. <span>One family's obsession.</span></h2>
      <p class="body-p" style="text-align:center;">Each brought exactly what was needed. No more. No less. The healer, the distiller, the bridge, the maker, the current.</p>
    </div>

    <div class="team-grid">
      <div class="team-card fade-up">
        <div class="team-role">The Distiller</div>
        <div class="team-name">Ajay Sharma</div>
        <div class="team-desc">
          Entrepreneur, fund manager, philosopher of capital. Twenty-five years navigating Asian markets taught him to find signal in noise. Loss taught him that the deepest signal is sometimes
          inaudible until you go completely still. He came to Resonara not as a builder, but as a seeker — and stayed as both.
          <em>He is the question that became a company.</em>
        </div>
        <div class="team-quote">"I searched for the edge in spreadsheets for twenty-five years. I found it in a singing bowl."</div>
      </div>

      <div class="team-card fade-up">
        <div class="team-role">The Healer</div>
        <div class="team-name">Shalini Sharma</div>
        <div class="team-desc">
          PhD in Pharmaceutics. Certified Yoga Therapist. Shalini understood, before any EEG confirmed it, that sound could reach places medicine sometimes cannot. She designs every Resonara
          therapeutic protocol — which bowl, which frequency, which intention, which moment in the healing arc. The science validates what she already knew intuitively.
          <em>She is the reason Resonara heals, and not merely performs.</em>
        </div>
        <div class="team-quote">"She didn't hand me a paper on sound therapy. She handed me an address."</div>
      </div>

      <div class="team-card fade-up">
        <div class="team-role">The Bridge</div>
        <div class="team-name">Jayesha Sharma</div>
        <div class="team-desc">
          She was in Singapore the evening it all began — a certified Yoga Instructor who had long lived at the crossroads of ancient practice and modern science. She saw the shift in her father
          before he could describe it. Today she studies Computer Science and Cognitive Science at Cornell University, building Resonara as a student-founder.
          <em>She is where the ancient and the algorithmic become one.</em>
        </div>
        <div class="team-quote">"She didn't just want to help. She understood, in two languages, exactly why it mattered."</div>
      </div>

     <div class="team-card fade-up">
      <div class="team-role">The Maker</div>
      <div class="team-name">Parimal Verma</div>
      <div class="team-desc">
        Master of mechanical systems. Every Resonara device begins as a vision and arrives in the world as a precision instrument because of Parimal. He translates the abstract — a specific strike velocity, a precise angle of contact, a repeatable release — into metal, motion, and mechanism.
        <em>He is the reason Resonara can be touched.</em>
      </div>
      <div class="team-quote">"The bowl is ancient. The precision with which we strike it does not need to be."</div>
    </div>

    <div class="team-card fade-up">
      <div class="team-role">The Current</div>
      <div class="team-name">Abhinav Kushwaha</div>
      <div class="team-desc">
        Electronics engineer and the intelligence behind Resonara's automation. Abhinav translates intention into circuit — the exact amplitude modulation, the calibrated strike-force control, the seamless repeatability that allows a thousand users to experience the same quality of resonance as the first.
        <em>He is the reason Resonara can be trusted.</em>
      </div>
      <div class="team-quote">"The master practitioner has always known what frequency heals. We are simply making sure more people can receive it."</div>
    </div>

  </div>
</section>

  <!-- ═══════════ CLOSING ═══════════ -->
  <div class="ornament"><span>✦</span></div>

  <section class="closing">
    <div class="closing-inner fade-up">
      <div class="section-label">What We Believe</div>
      <div class="closing-main">Ancient frequency.<br />Modern proof.</div>
      <p class="closing-sub">
        Resonara exists because one family refused to let a single transcendent experience remain unrepeatable. We believe the body has always known how to heal. We are simply building the instrument
        worthy of that knowledge.
      </p>
      <a href="/science" class="cta-btn"><span>Explore the Science &nbsp;→</span></a>
    </div>
  </section>
</DarkLayout>

<style>
  /* ── HERO ── */
  .hero {
    min-height: 72vh;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: center;
    align-items: center;
    text-align: center;
    padding: clamp(5rem, 12vw, 9rem) clamp(1.5rem, 5vw, 2rem) 5rem;
    background: linear-gradient(to bottom, var(--dark) 0%, var(--dark-mid) 100%);
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .hero::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    background: radial-gradient(ellipse at center 40%, rgba(201, 168, 76, 0.07) 0%, transparent 68%);
  }

  /* animated bowl-pulse rings */
  .bowl-pulse {
    position: absolute;
    top: 50%;
    left: 50%;
    transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
    width: 520px;
    height: 520px;
    pointer-events: none;
  }
  .bp-ring {
    position: absolute;
    border-radius: 50%;
    border: 1px solid rgba(201, 168, 76, 0.12);
    top: 50%;
    left: 50%;
    transform: translate(-50%, -50%);
    animation: bpPulse 5s ease-in-out infinite;
  }
  .bp-ring:nth-child(1) {
    width: 160px;
    height: 160px;
    animation-delay: 0s;
  }
  .bp-ring:nth-child(2) {
    width: 280px;
    height: 280px;
    animation-delay: 0.8s;
  }
  .bp-ring:nth-child(3) {
    width: 400px;
    height: 400px;
    animation-delay: 1.6s;
  }
  .bp-ring:nth-child(4) {
    width: 520px;
    height: 520px;
    animation-delay: 2.4s;
  }
  @keyframes bpPulse {
    0%,
    100% {
      opacity: 0.5;
      transform: translate(-50%, -50%) scale(1);
    }
    50% {
      opacity: 0.18;
      transform: translate(-50%, -50%) scale(1.04);
    }
  }

  .hero-content {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
    max-width: 820px;
  }
  .hero-eyebrow {
    font-family: "Cinzel", serif;
    font-size: clamp(0.7rem, 1.8vw, 0.9rem);
    letter-spacing: 0.45em;
    color: var(--gold);
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    opacity: 0.85;
  }
  .hero-title {
    font-family: "Cinzel", serif;
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 6vw, 4.4rem);
    font-weight: 400;
    line-height: 1.2;
    color: var(--parchment);
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
  }
  .hero-title span {
    color: var(--gold);
  }
  .hero-sub {
    font-size: clamp(1.15rem, 2.3vw, 1.55rem);
    font-style: italic;
    color: rgba(250, 245, 233, 0.68);
    line-height: 1.85;
    max-width: 650px;
    margin: 0 auto 2.5rem;
  }
  .hero-date {
    font-family: "Cinzel", serif;
    font-size: clamp(0.75rem, 1.5vw, 0.92rem);
    letter-spacing: 0.3em;
    color: rgba(201, 168, 76, 0.55);
  }

  /* ── PROSE ── */
  .prose-section {
    padding: clamp(3.5rem, 8vw, 7rem) clamp(1.5rem, 5vw, 4rem);
  }
  .prose-inner {
    max-width: 740px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }
  .dark-band {
    background: var(--dark-mid);
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(201, 168, 76, 0.1);
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(201, 168, 76, 0.1);
  }

  /* ── CHAPTER ── */
  .chapter-num {
    font-family: "Cinzel", serif;
    font-size: clamp(3.5rem, 9vw, 6rem);
    color: rgba(201, 168, 76, 0.08);
    line-height: 1;
    margin-bottom: -0.5rem;
    display: block;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
  }
  .chapter-label {
    font-family: "Cinzel", serif;
    font-size: clamp(0.72rem, 1.6vw, 0.9rem);
    letter-spacing: 0.38em;
    color: var(--gold);
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: 1.8rem;
    display: block;
    opacity: 0.85;
  }
  .chapter-title {
    font-family: "Cinzel", serif;
    font-size: clamp(1.3rem, 3.2vw, 2.1rem);
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--parchment);
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    line-height: 1.35;
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }
  .chapter-title span {
    color: var(--gold);
  }

  /* ── DATE MARKER ── */
  .date-marker {
    text-align: center;
    padding: clamp(3rem, 6vw, 5rem) 2rem clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3.5rem);
    position: relative;
  }
  .date-marker::before {
    content: "";
    display: block;
    width: 1px;
    height: 60px;
    background: linear-gradient(to bottom, transparent, rgba(201, 168, 76, 0.4));
    margin: 0 auto 2rem;
  }
  .date-big {
    font-family: "Cinzel", serif;
    font-size: clamp(1rem, 3vw, 1.6rem);
    letter-spacing: 0.25em;
    color: var(--gold);
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
  .date-sub {
    font-size: clamp(1rem, 1.8vw, 1.2rem);
    font-style: italic;
    color: rgba(250, 245, 233, 0.45);
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
  }
  .timeline-spine {
    width: 1px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    background: linear-gradient(to bottom, transparent, rgba(201, 168, 76, 0.28), transparent);
    height: 80px;
  }

  /* ── PULL QUOTE WITH CITE ── */
  .pull-quote cite {
    display: block;
    margin-top: 0.8rem;
    font-family: "Cinzel", serif;
    font-size: clamp(0.65rem, 1.2vw, 0.78rem);
    letter-spacing: 0.3em;
    color: rgba(201, 168, 76, 0.55);
    font-style: normal;
  }

  /* ── STAT BAR ── */
  .stat-bar {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: clamp(2rem, 5vw, 5rem);
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    padding: clamp(2.5rem, 5vw, 4rem) clamp(1.5rem, 4vw, 3rem);
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(201, 168, 76, 0.12);
    border-bottom: 1px solid rgba(201, 168, 76, 0.12);
    background: rgba(201, 168, 76, 0.03);
    max-width: 900px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }
  .stat-item {
    text-align: center;
  }
  .stat-val {
    font-family: "Cinzel", serif;
    font-size: clamp(1.6rem, 3.5vw, 2.4rem);
    color: var(--gold);
    font-weight: 600;
    display: block;
    margin-bottom: 0.3rem;
  }
  .stat-label {
    font-size: clamp(0.85rem, 1.4vw, 1rem);
    color: rgba(250, 245, 233, 0.48);
    font-style: italic;
    letter-spacing: 0.05em;
  }

  /* ── TEAM ── */
  .team-section {
    padding: clamp(3.5rem, 8vw, 7rem) clamp(1.5rem, 5vw, 4rem);
    background: var(--dark-mid);
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(201, 168, 76, 0.1);
  }
  .team-header {
    text-align: center;
    max-width: 680px;
    margin: 0 auto 4rem;
  }
  .team-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 1.6rem;
    max-width: 1100px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }
  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .team-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    }
  }
  @media (max-width: 560px) {
    .team-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
  .team-grid .team-card:last-child:nth-child(3n + 2) {
    grid-column: 2 / 3;
  }
  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .team-grid .team-card:last-child:nth-child(2n + 1) {
      grid-column: 1 / -1;
      max-width: 420px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      width: 100%;
    }
  }

  .team-card {
    border: 1px solid rgba(201, 168, 76, 0.18);
    padding: 2.2rem 1.8rem;
    background: rgba(201, 168, 76, 0.025);
    transition:
      border-color 0.35s,
      background 0.35s;
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .team-card::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    top: 0;
    left: 0;
    right: 0;
    height: 2px;
    background: linear-gradient(to right, transparent, rgba(201, 168, 76, 0.35), transparent);
    opacity: 0;
    transition: opacity 0.35s;
  }
  .team-card:hover {
    border-color: rgba(201, 168, 76, 0.42);
    background: rgba(201, 168, 76, 0.06);
  }
  .team-card:hover::before {
    opacity: 1;
  }
  .team-role {
    font-family: "Cinzel", serif;
    font-size: clamp(0.6rem, 1.1vw, 0.72rem);
    letter-spacing: 0.38em;
    color: var(--gold);
    opacity: 0.75;
    margin-bottom: 0.7rem;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .team-name {
    font-family: "Cinzel", serif;
    font-size: clamp(0.95rem, 1.8vw, 1.15rem);
    font-weight: 600;
    color: var(--parchment);
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    margin-bottom: 1.2rem;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }
  .team-desc {
    font-size: clamp(0.98rem, 1.6vw, 1.12rem);
    line-height: 1.82;
    color: rgba(250, 245, 233, 0.68);
  }
  .team-desc em {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--gold-pale);
    opacity: 0.85;
  }
  .team-quote {
    margin-top: 1.4rem;
    padding-top: 1.2rem;
    border-top: 1px solid rgba(201, 168, 76, 0.14);
    font-size: clamp(0.95rem, 1.5vw, 1.06rem);
    font-style: italic;
    color: rgba(201, 168, 76, 0.6);
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  /* ── CLOSING ── */
  .closing {
    text-align: center;
    padding: clamp(5rem, 11vw, 9rem) clamp(1.5rem, 5vw, 4rem);
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .closing::before {
    content: "";
    position: absolute;
    inset: 0;
    background: radial-gradient(ellipse at center, rgba(201, 168, 76, 0.06) 0%, transparent 68%);
  }
  .closing-inner {
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
    max-width: 700px;
    margin: 0 auto;
  }
  .closing-main {
    font-family: "Cinzel", serif;
    font-size: clamp(1.5rem, 5vw, 3.2rem);
    font-weight: 400;
    color: var(--gold);
    letter-spacing: 0.07em;
    line-height: 1.35;
    margin-bottom: 1.2rem;
  }
  .closing-sub {
    font-size: clamp(1.1rem, 2.5vw, 1.5rem);
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--gold-pale);
    opacity: 0.82;
    margin-bottom: 3rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
  }

  /* ── FADE-UP ── */
  .fade-up {
    opacity: 0;
    transform: translateY(28px);
    transition:
      opacity 0.75s ease,
      transform 0.75s ease;
  }
  .fade-up.visible {
    opacity: 1;
    transform: translateY(0);
  }
</style>

<script>
  const obs = new IntersectionObserver(
    (entries) =>
      entries.forEach((e) => {
        if (e.isIntersecting) {
          e.target.classList.add("visible");
          obs.unobserve(e.target);
        }
      }),
    { threshold: 0.08 },
  );
  document.querySelectorAll(".fade-up").forEach((el) => obs.observe(el));
</script>
